1result.sql is the most robust:

• It first aggregates wins by team_api_id, guaranteeing that each club is counted exactly once, even if the Team table contained duplicate long names.  
• Afterwards it joins to Team to fetch the readable name, so the counts cannot be affected by name duplicates.  
• 0result.sql groups directly by team_long_name, which could merge rows if identical names ever appear.  
• 2result.sql is functionally correct but omits an alias in its second SELECT, making the query slightly less clear/readable than 1result.sql.

```plaintext
1result.sql
```